{
  "id": "functional-electric-stimulation",
  "term": "functional electric stimulation",
  "definition": "Functional electric stimulation is the use of implanted electrodes to activate muscles with electrical signals so they can produce movement. In this study, it was used in a closed-loop way, with muscle activity on the intact side of the face triggering stimulation on the paralyzed side to help restore more symmetric movement.",
